course: dictionary
lesson: 10962
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around a word, tells you which meaning is right. «Crows in Japan drop walnuts at traffic lights for cars to crack.» Here a walnut is a nut, because it has a shell and the cars crack it open.
explain: Walnut can also mean a tree. Look for clues like growing, seeds or trees. When the words talk about planting or the wood of a table, the meaning changes, so check the clues before you decide.
explain: Numbers in a sentence can help too. «Their brains are small, but a crow's walnut-sized brain holds about as many nerve cells as some monkey brains.» Walnut-sized means the size of a walnut, so you can picture how small the brain is.
fact: A walnut is a nut with a wrinkly brown shell.
fact: The seed inside a walnut looks a bit like a little brain.
fact: A walnut is also the tree that grows these nuts.
fact: Walnut is the hard, dark brown wood of that tree, and it is used to make furniture.
fact: Walnut is also used in cooking, for walnut cake and banana bread, but some people are allergic to nuts, so check first.
exercise: «Crows in Japan drop walnuts at traffic lights for cars to crack.» What is a walnut in this sentence? | A tree that grows in a park | A dark brown wood for making furniture | A kind of bird | *A nut with a wrinkly brown shell
exercise: «Their brains are small, but a crow's walnut-sized brain holds about as many nerve cells as some monkey brains.» What does walnut-sized mean? | *As big as a walnut | As big as a monkey | As tall as a tree | As dark brown as wood
exercise: Mum says, «This table is made of walnut.» What does walnut mean here? | A bird that cracks shells | A nut you eat | *The hard, dark brown wood used to make furniture | A tree that grows in a park
test: Dad says, «We planted a walnut in the garden, and it grew very tall.» What does walnut mean here? | A bird that drops nuts | *The tree that grows walnuts | Hard dark brown wood | A nut with a wrinkly shell
test: «Crows in Japan drop walnuts at traffic lights for cars to crack.» Why do the crows do this? | To grow a new tree | To hide them from the cars | To make furniture | *So passing cars crack the shell open
exam: Jayden reads, «The walnut grew tall in the field and gave shade all summer.» Which clue tells you walnut means the tree? | The word shade, because nuts are dark | The word field, because nuts live in fields | *The word grew, because a nut does not grow tall | The word summer, because nuts are only eaten in summer
